# The E5's 9-key keypad has no Enter: its confirm key -- matrix row 1, column 0,
# i.e. scancode 8 (MATRIX_SCAN_CODE(row, col, 3) with 4 rows x 7 columns) -- emits
# KEY_SELECT, which nothing in the session handles.  phosh's lock screen has no
# unlock key of its own (its on-screen keypad is 3x4 with [OSK] [0] [backspace]),
# so a PIN typed on the physical keypad could never be submitted; it becomes
# KP_Enter here, which is what the lock screen accepts.
#
# The scancode is the *matrix scan code* (8), not the keycode it produces (353):
# evdev's EVIOCSKEYCODE indexes dev->keycode[], whose size is rows*cols (28), and
# an index of 353 is out of range and fails with EINVAL -- the mistake that once
# made this look like "the keypad cannot be remapped at all".
# tools/keycode-query.py reads and writes exactly this map.
#
# The back key (scancode 0) is deliberately *not* remapped: KEY_BACK is what the
# session uses for "back", and the lock screen has an on-screen backspace.
#
# /etc lives in the initramfs overlay and is rewritten on every boot;
# systemd-hwdb-update.service (WantedBy=sysinit.target) recompiles
# /etc/udev/hwdb.bin when this file is newer, and udev's keyboard builtin applies
# the mapping when the keypad device appears.
evdev:input:b0000v0000p0000e0000*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_8=kpenter
